---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'; import ToolApp from '../components/ToolApp.astro';
import { breadcrumbSchema, softwareSchema } from '../lib/schema';
import { generateDome } from '../core/geometry';
const title='Minecraft Dome Generator – Layer-by-Layer Block Blueprint | VoxelCurve';
const description='Generate Minecraft domes layer by layer with exact row segments, material counts and guided build progress. Create low, hemispherical or tall domes.';
const presets=[
  {width:15,depth:15,height:8},
  {width:21,depth:21,height:11},
  {width:31,depth:31,height:16}
].map(p=>({...p,blocks:generateDome(p.width,p.depth,p.height,'thin',1).blockCount}));
const schemas=[
  breadcrumbSchema([{name:'VoxelCurve',url:'https://voxelcurve.com/'},{name:'Minecraft Dome Generator',url:'https://voxelcurve.com/minecraft-dome-generator'}]),
  softwareSchema({name:'VoxelCurve Minecraft Dome Generator',url:'https://voxelcurve.com/minecraft-dome-generator',description,featureList:['Layer-by-layer dome blueprint','Hollow and filled domes','Guided row and segment building','Material count','PNG export','Litematic export']})
];
---
<BaseLayout {title} {description} canonical="https://voxelcurve.com/minecraft-dome-generator" {schemas}>
<section class="product-stage">
  <div class="hero container"><span class="eyebrow">Layer-by-layer builder</span><div class="hero-grid"><div><h1>Minecraft Dome Generator</h1><p>Generate a hollow or filled dome and build it one layer, row and segment at a time.</p></div><div class="hero-side-note"><span class="mono-label">LAYERED GEOMETRY</span><strong>Plan every layer</strong><span>Track the current layer, row and segment while you build.</span></div></div></div>
  <ToolApp shape="dome" />
  <div class="product-proof container"><div><b>LAYER GUIDE</b><span>Exact row segments for every height.</span></div><div><b>HOLLOW / FILLED</b><span>True shell or solid dome geometry.</span></div><div><b>LOCAL PROGRESS</b><span>Resume from the same browser.</span></div><div><b>EXPORT READY</b><span>PNG, TXT and Litematic workflow.</span></div></div>
</section>
<section class="section"><div class="container prose"><h2>Build a Minecraft dome without losing your layer</h2><p>VoxelCurve represents a dome as an upper ellipsoid. Each horizontal layer is broken into rows and exact block segments, so the same blueprint can guide both small roofs and large survival builds. Whether you think of it as a Minecraft dome generator, dome maker or dome creator, the output is the same layer-by-layer construction plan.</p><h2>Hemisphere, low dome or tall dome</h2><p>Width and depth define the footprint. Height controls the profile. Use the hemisphere shortcut for a classic half-sphere, reduce height for a flatter roof, or increase it for a taller elliptical dome.</p><h2>Hollow domes are true shells</h2><p>The hollow mode subtracts an inner ellipsoid from the outer structure instead of simply drawing a thin circle on every layer. That keeps the cap and upper layers structurally consistent.</p><h2>Layer navigation</h2><p>The guided builder tracks the current layer, row and segment. Complete a segment and VoxelCurve moves to the next instruction while keeping progress in your current browser.</p></div></section>
<section class="section preset-section"><div class="container"><div class="section-kicker">Common dome presets</div><div class="section-split"><div><h2>Useful starting dimensions</h2><p class="section-intro">These hemisphere-style presets use a one-block hollow shell. Open one directly, then adjust the dimensions if needed.</p></div><div class="preset-table">{presets.map(p=><a class="preset-row" href={`/minecraft-dome-generator#d-${p.width}-${p.depth}-${p.height}-thin-1`}><span class="preset-dim">{p.width}×{p.depth}×{p.height}</span><span>{p.blocks.toLocaleString()} blocks</span><span class="size-action">Open →</span></a>)}</div></div></div></section>
<section class="section related-section"><div class="container"><div class="section-kicker">Related tools</div><h2>Keep building</h2><div class="related-list"><a href="/"><span class="related-index">01</span><div><h3>Circle Generator</h3><p>Plan the footprint of circular towers and roofs.</p></div><span class="related-arrow">↗</span></a><a href="/minecraft-oval-generator"><span class="related-index">02</span><div><h3>Oval Generator</h3><p>Create elliptical footprints for elongated domes.</p></div><span class="related-arrow">↗</span></a><a href="/how-to-make-a-circle-in-minecraft"><span class="related-index">03</span><div><h3>Circle Guide</h3><p>Learn anchors, symmetry and the row-segment construction method.</p></div><span class="related-arrow">↗</span></a></div></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="container prose">
  <h2>Minecraft dome guide: from footprint to roof</h2>
  <p>Build the bottom layer first, confirm its center and orientation, then advance upward one layer at a time. Follow each row's start offset and segment length, mark completed work and check the remaining materials before continuing.</p>
  <h3>Can the Minecraft dome maker plan an observatory roof?</h3>
  <p>Yes. Match the width and depth to the supporting walls, then choose a height that leaves enough room inside. Use a hollow shell for an open interior. For a round MC dome, keep width and depth equal.</p>
  <h3>How do I make a flatter roof?</h3>
  <p>Reduce the height while keeping the footprint fixed. A Minecraft dome creator resolves each smaller upper layer, so follow the generated rows instead of repeating the base outline at every height.</p>
  <h3>Does a dome generator Minecraft builders use place the roof automatically?</h3>
  <p>No. VoxelCurve supplies a placement plan and local progress tracking. If you need a “Minecraft how to build a dome” walkthrough, follow the layer sequence above; a compatible Java tool is required to use the optional Litematic export.</p>
</div></section>
</BaseLayout>
